  - B03.CH11.P02.S03 — Caps: exception pressure, near-cap clustering, and elite splitting
  - B03.CH11.P02.S04 — R/B: timing asymmetry, local burden concentration, swing backlash
  - B03.CH11.P02.S05 — Measurement and audit layer: definition shifting, uncertainty, perceived technocracy

- B03.CH11.P03 — Conflict modes: types of internal conflict and their signatures
  - B03.CH11.P03.S01 — Parametric conflict: thresholds/tempo/priorities within the rails
  - B03.CH11.P03.S02 — Interpretive conflict: classification (E vs productive), boundary rules, exposure tests
  - B03.CH11.P03.S03 — Institutional conflict: authorities, audit findings, sanctions
  - B03.CH11.P03.S04 — Legitimacy conflict: mandate claims, representation, procedural fairness
  - B03.CH11.P03.S05 — Existential rupture: attack on non-negotiables (caps/commons/auditability)

- B03.CH11.P04 — Schism and split dynamics: when conflict becomes a fork
  - B03.CH11.P04.S01 — Triggers: exception explosion, sanction-rate collapse, black-box allocation
  - B03.CH11.P04.S02 — Coalition rupture: swing groups lose, scapegoating, media capture
  - B03.CH11.P04.S03 — Elite splitting: production vs finance, platform power vs commons
  - B03.CH11.P04.S04 — Crisis windows: shocks as accelerators of rupture
  - B03.CH11.P04.S05 — Fork protocol: classification, name label, and compatibility status (link to B03.CH07)

