## B03.CH12 — Closing: democratic consistency test and governance metrics

- B03.CH12.P01 — Purpose and scope: democratic consistency test as the capstone (pass/fail + escalation)
  - B03.CH12.P01.S01 — Function: detection of drift, capture, and regression within OBA governance
  - B03.CH12.P01.S02 — Delimitation: the test assesses governance, not sector-by-sector policy content
  - B03.CH12.P01.S03 — Relations: inputs from Book 1/2/4 (measurability, transition, information order)
  - B03.CH12.P01.S04 — Machine-readability: fixed inputs, outputs, version IDs, and thresholds

- B03.CH12.P02 — Non-negotiables in democratic form: minimum procedural requirements
  - B03.CH12.P02.S01 — Separation of functions: execution, audit, oversight, judicial review (no role mixing)
  - B03.CH12.P02.S02 — Contestability: objection/appeal, access to evidence, non-sabotage defaults
  - B03.CH12.P02.S03 — Transparency minimum: definition sets, registers, dashboards, changelog discipline
  - B03.CH12.P02.S04 — Exception discipline: sunsets, rollback, non-stackability, impact registration
  - B03.CH12.P02.S05 — Anti-overreach: prohibited linkages and proportionality rails (privacy/control)

- B03.CH12.P03 — Governance metrics (minimum set): what is continuously measured
  - B03.CH12.P03.S01 — Capture metrics: vendor concentration, revolving-door incidents, lobby-disclosure compliance
  - B03.CH12.P03.S02 — Enforcement metric: sanction rate, enforcement latency, recidivism rate, exception stacking
  - B03.CH12.P03.S03 — Epistemic metric: reproducibility, audit coverage, model/rule churn, restatement frequency
  - B03.CH12.P03.S04 — Representation metric: participation bias, inclusion, churn in commons representation
  - B03.CH12.P03.S05 — Legitimacy metric: trust/acceptance (proxies), complaint volumes, appeal outcomes, procedural fairness

- B03.CH12.P04 — Early-warning indicators: drift signatures and thresholds
  - B03.CH12.P04.S01 — Semantic drift: definition shifting without changelog, metric-bridging gaps
  - B03.CH12.P04.S02 — Exception drift: exception ratio↑, renewals↑, selectivity↑, sunset failure
  - B03.CH12.P04.S03 — Black-box drift: declining contestability, closed computation rules, audit refusal patterns
  - B03.CH12.P04.S04 — Capture drift: vendor lock-in signals, single-source procurement, audit interference
  - B03.CH12.P04.S05 — Authoritarian drift: surveillance expansion, selective enforcement, emergency normalisation

- B03.CH12.P05 — Response ladder: what follows from signals (automatic and political)
  - B03.CH12.P05.S01 — Trigger → enhanced audit mode: scope expansion, forensic access, parallel review
  - B03.CH12.P05.S02 — Correction → requalification/rollback: reverse decisions, contracts, tooling, and exceptions
  - B03.CH12.P05.S03 — Hard stops: suspend allocations/decisions under black-box governance or measurement uncertainty
  - B03.CH12.P05.S04 — Governance reset: rotation, reconstitution, second-source tooling, procurement reset
  - B03.CH12.P05.S05 — Re-authorisation: new mandate for a constitutive deviation (incl. fork classification)

- B03.CH12.P06 — Public reporting and accountability: output formats of the test
  - B03.CH12.P06.S01 — Consistency report: scorecard per metric, thresholds, trend, status label
  - B03.CH12.P06.S02 — Incident reporting: root cause, implicated decisions, exception log, recovery plan
  - B03.CH12.P06.S03 — Changelog discipline: rationale, impact analysis, backward compatibility where possible
  - B03.CH12.P06.S04 — Restatements: transparent corrections and bridging of historical series
  - B03.CH12.P06.S05 — Audit of the test: independent review of methodology and tooling

- B03.CH12.P07 — Fork and compatibility outcome: when it formally deviates
  - B03.CH12.P07.S01 — Compatible: all non-negotiables intact; variation purely parametric
  - B03.CH12.P07.S02 — Partially compatible: temporary emergency deviation with hard sunsets/rollback and evidence discipline
  - B03.CH12.P07.S03 — Incompatible: structural cap erosion, black-box governance, or permanent exception explosion
  - B03.CH12.P07.S04 — Label and naming rule: mandatory relabeling upon incompatibility
  - B03.CH12.P07.S05 — Handover: inputs to Book 2/4 for transition and cognitive consistency tests


